WEBVTT

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:04.600
And so, let's all have a listen.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.270
Dear Hell...

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:14.610
Jigoku mitai ni asobitai
I want to have a good time like Hell

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:19.790
Jigoku mitai ni yasumitai
I want to rest like Hell

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:24.580
Jigoku mitai na nidoneshite
I want to go back to sleep like Hell

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:29.170
Teiji de agaritai
And finish work on time

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:35.010
Jigoku mitai ni tabesugite
I ate too much like Hell

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:39.720
Jigoku mitai ni nomisugita
I drank too much like Hell

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:45.020
Aa sonna wake de
Ah, for these reasons

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:50.280
Jigoku mitai
It's like Hell

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.690
Sonna toki koso deban desu
At such a time it's all the more his turn on stage

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.360
Hoozuki-sama ga moriageru
Mr. Hozuki livens things up

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:57.450
Omakase kudasai!
Please leave it to me!

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:03.040
Aa jigoku jigoku mainichi jigoku
Ah, Hell, Hell, every day Hell

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.620
Jigoku jigoku
Hell, Hell

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.290
"Uso desho?!"
"You can't mean that, right?!"

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:13.210
Jigoku jigoku youkoso jigoku
Hell, Hell, welcome to Hell

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:14.050
Atchi muite
Look that way

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:14.630
Kotchi muite
Look this way

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:15.760
Abikyoukan!
Pandemonium!

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.050
Gongo! Doudan!
What the hell!

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.640
Shitsureishimashita!
Pardon me!

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:23.560
Sonna kanji no
In that kind of way

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.940
A! Jigoku desu! Jajajajan!
Ah! It's Hell! Ta ta ta-da!

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.020
Katsu!
Curses!

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:40.450
Long, long ago, when Okuninushi-no-Mikoto
ruled the Mundane World,

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:49.540
the great celestial sun goddess suddenly said,
"The land should be ruled by my children."

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:55.050
Okuninushi
no
Mikoto's
Daughter

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.670
Although she then sent
envoy after envoy to the surface...

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:03.470
...the envoys all ended up staying
by Okuninushi-no-Mikoto's side.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:08.520
The troubled great sun goddess dispatched a pheasant
named Nakime and had her admonish the envoys.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:13.360
Nakime

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.650
The troubled great sun goddess dispatched a pheasant
named Nakime and had her admonish the envoys.
Do your job! Do your job!

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.320
Do your job! Do your job!

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:17.610
But a perverse goddess named
Amanosagume enticed the envoys.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:19.240
Kill it with an arrow!

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.780
And the pheasant was killed.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:30.040
This goddess called Amanosagume later began
to develop into a yokai known as Amanojaku.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:38.130
AMANOJAKU

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.600
Think they'll be sentenced to Hell?

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.690
Don't say that so cheerfully!

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:55.020
The Offices of Enma hereby sentence you to Inferno Hell!

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:59.490
Reflect on your excessively perverse nature!

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.870
"Inferno Hell"...

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.700
That concludes the trial!

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:07.830
Mr. Hozuki!

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.790
Inferno Hell is the hell you go to for sins
that stem from holding evil views.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.420
"Evil views"?

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:23.550
DRAGON REVOLVING REALM:
THE HELL FOR THOSE

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:23.550
WHO HAVE BAD MANNERS AND ARE RUDE
INFERNO HELL
INSECT JUMBLE REALM:
THE HELL FOR THOSE WHO SHOW
ZERO IMPROVEMENT EVEN AFTER
BEING WARNED ABOUT THEIR MISDEEDS

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.630
In short, these are sins that are wicked,

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:22.140
go against reason, or that act to incite people.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:28.020
This hell is also known as Amanojaku's Den.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:31.850
Subjectively speaking, it's a rather difficult hell,

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.980
but people end up there by causing
tremendous harm or annoyance.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.150
Ah, that's right. I've remembered something.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:44.410
One of the Hell minions from Inferno Hell
said she'd like to meet to you, Rurio.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:45.990
Meet me?

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.580
A Hell minion bird, by chance?

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.210
Nope, a human woman.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.460
Ah, wait... I guess there's a bird, too.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:56.920
Hm?

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:05.390
INFERNO
HELL

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.730
Oh, I see!

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.730
I suppose any mention of Amanojaku
does bring to mind Princess Uriko.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.480
I'm impressed you figured that out.

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:18.400
Oh, I can tell. She looks the part, after all.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:24.200
BEST
IN
JAPAN

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:22.360
I wonder if it's a characteristic
of people born from plants...

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:26.530
Momotaro played up his status as
a "peach human" from head to toe, after all.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:29.410
BEST
IN
JAPAN
PEACH-COLORED

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:29.330
I mean, even his kimono was peach colored.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:32.540
Pheasant! Are you Momotaro's pheasant?!

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:34.500
Nice to meet you, comrade!

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.040
Nice to meet you, comrade!
Wh-wh-what?! What's this now?!

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.130
Wh-wh-what?! What's this now?!

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.710
We were both killed by Amanojaku.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.880
What do you say we try becoming friends?

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.840
Uh... Oh?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:49.470
Ah, you must be talking the story of
Okuninushi-no-Mikoto and the great sun goddess.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.430
I'm not actually Nakime, you know.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.480
However, you are a divine-messenger bird
who has a long-standing tie to Amanojaku,

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.940
as well as being the bird
who defeated the evil demon, Onki!

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:05.530
I was born from a melon.
So, I felt a strong affinity with Momotaro.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.410
So that's what made you want to meet me, huh?

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.740
Hmm, that makes sense. Very interesting...

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.160
You're a princess born from a melon.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.630
And I, as companion of a man born from a peach,
subjugated a band of ogres.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:25.220
The peach tree has been recognized by Izanaki
as a tree that drives away ill will.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:30.760
And Izanaki is the sun goddess's father, right?

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:37.310
And the sun goddess's divine-messenger pheasant
was long ago killed by Amanojaku.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:41.860
Then I, another pheasant, subjugated the ogres...

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:45.780
This is kind of like a word-association game, huh?

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:50.200
So, about that Nakime...
Isn't she probably one of Rurio's ancestors?

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.990
Huh? Why do you think that?

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:56.330
I mean, for a pheasant, you sure think deeply
about lots of stuff, you know?

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:59.170
So just now you decide to point that out, huh?

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.380
Actually, I think he's right.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.800
There's a high probability that Shiro
is a white divine-messenger dog.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:11.010
Kakisuke is a monkey who, after the Monkey-Crab
Incident and with the blessing of Mr. Jizo,

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:14.430
atoned for his sins by working
as Momotaro's companion...

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.520
That is what you said earlier, isn't it?

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:17.600
Uh, yes!

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:22.770
In that case, Rurio, it makes more sense
to think of you as a pheasant touched by the divine.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:27.490
Perhaps Momotaro, a tentatively divine
superhuman man who was born from a peach,

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:30.910
ILL WILL
ILL WILL

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:32.330
had the power to beckon companions
with a knack for repelling ill will.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:37.790
Woo-hoo! Momotaro is touched by the divine!

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.500
Even looking the way he does!

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:45.050
Well, the instant he beckoned you, I'm not so sure
he was touched by the divine any longer.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.300
Still, if that is the case, it makes me proud.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:54.850
I don't fully get it, but my old family motto was:
"Watch out for lies and arrows."

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.350
Oh, it figures!

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.640
See?!

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.810
O Descendant of Nakime, come and render futile
the perverse dead together with me!

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:04.020
O Descendant of Nakime, come and render futile
the perverse dead together with me!
Ah, w-wait a minute... y-you're-

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.860
It is with that sole desire
that I took my current position here!

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.740
Looks like that woman subscribes
to the same school of thought as Miss Mustard...

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.820
Those kinds of people tend to flock together, don't they?

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.830
So, you say that you were killed by Amanojaku?

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:18.870
How epic.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:20.080
Yes.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:22.460
Hey, I haven't heard the story.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:27.250
PRINCESS
URIKO

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:26.920
Princess Uriko.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:33.260
Long, long ago, when an old man and an old woman
cut open a melon they had picked up in a river,

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.640
a cute baby girl was born from inside.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.020
This sounds pretty familiar.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:40.810
Shush!

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:44.940
The beauty of this Princess Uriko, who had been born
from a melon, became the talk of the town.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:48.650
Talk of marriage to a certain feudal lord soon arose.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:56.120
On the other hand, Amanojaku, a killjoy who's always
up to no good, was not pleased by the news.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:00.910
How could this be? That damn girl's ugly as hell!

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.380
Amanojaku killed Princess Uriko.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:08.170
She then dressed herself in the
princess's skin and impersonated her.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:11.880
However, the princess's determined soul became a bird.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:14.050
That thing there is Amanojaku!

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:23.230
Amanojaku was showered with blows by
the enraged old man and woman and then died, you see.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:27.190
So you became a bird, huh?

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:30.400
That's right. My remorse transformed into a bird.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:36.320
So, I guess this Amanojaku
both killed and got killed by a bird, huh?

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:37.870
That's right.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:41.790
More surprising still, Amanojaku was actually a woman?

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:46.210
She and Amanosagume, who killed the pheasant,
are the very same person.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:50.340
She's a liar who's malicious at heart.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:54.260
So is there any chance she ended up in this hell, too?

00:08:55.220 --> 00:09:00.770
Despite it all, she's actually a goddess,
so unfortunately she's not subject to receiving judgment.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.640
Still, she's here - this very moment, in fact.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.400
I'm having her work here to atone for her sins.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:12.030
It seems that upon becoming employed,
her disposition became somewhat more cheerful.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.700
Mr. Hozuki~

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:22.500
Mr. Hozuki... you call me?

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.290
YIKES!

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.300
Princess Uriko, I see you're as ugly as ever!

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.800
It's fine that she's become a bit more cheerful, but...

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:39.510
Aaahh... So this is what happens
when Amanojaku gets a bit of self-confidence?

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:45.140
Huh? What? What? Everyone came here to see Ameno?

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:48.980
Oh my, I feel so embarrassed!

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:52.110
EEEEEEEEEEEK!

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:56.780
Y-you... killed Princess Uriko, didn't you?

00:09:57.070 --> 00:10:01.780
I mean, don't you think the idea of this uggo
marrying a feudal lord is messed up?!

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:04.620
Ameno did nothing wrong!

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:08.870
It's in her nature to irritate people,

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:13.380
and with the introduction of the Internet,
her disposition only became worse.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:15.340
Makes sense...

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.840
Currently her favorite activity is...

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.470
flaming.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.350
No surprise there...

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:29.400
By her nature, Amanosagume has the power
to see into people's hearts and perceive their thoughts.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:36.780
However, because of her twisted personality,
she's always using that power to entrap people.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:41.240
That has been used to turn the tables on her,
and now she finds herself here as a hell minion.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:48.210
That's right... Mr. Hozuki really pressured me into it...

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:53.540
Ameno... did turn him down at first, though.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:56.130
Well, I suppose I had no choice.

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:59.630
She has a propensity to lie, so please just ignore her.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:05.640
Amazing... It's like no matter
what you say to her, it's pointless.

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:10.480
With her around, it's possible
to subject the dead to limitless stress.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:11.980
Huh?

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:15.320
Princess Uriko, what you mad about?

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:18.110
No use in fussing about the past, right?

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:20.740
You sure are stubborn, you know?

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.700
The pain's killing me...

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.160
"ThE pAin's kiLLing mE..."

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:30.830
Don't imitate me...

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:34.210
"DOn't iMITate Me... DOn't iMITate Me..."

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:38.630
The more irritated they get,
the more they fan the flames, you see.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:44.510
In a sense, she is the most talented of all
at getting on the nerves of Inferno Hell's dead.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:47.390
Only someone like you could anticipate
she'd have that effect.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.810
Ah, a pheasant!

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:51.850
A photo! Photo time!

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.940
Long ago, I killed a pheasant, you know.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:58.400
That thing was so noisy up in its tree.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:02.240
"The pheasant wouldn't be shot but for its cries."
You'd think that'd be common sense...

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.160
Must've been stupid.

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:06.990
I sure do hate birds.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:10.660
I got a cute photo!

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:15.000
Rocket... LAUNCHER!

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:24.550
Wow!

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:30.640
O Descendant of Nakime, I see you avenged your
long-standing grudge in the form of a fated arrow!

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:34.350
Hey, Pheasant, what you angry about?!

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.610
"Long-standing," you say...

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:41.360
Actually, she got under my skin
within 10 minutes of meeting her.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:56.670
Um, perhaps...

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:05.090
Is getting stuck in a spot like that seriously a thing...?

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:12.020
People sometimes meaninglessly stick a finger
into a bottle and can't get it back out, right?

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.560
That does happen...

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:18.900
Thank you kindly for rescuing me.

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:21.900
Tell me, who are you and where do you come from?

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:25.990
I'm Hozuki, First Chief of Staff at the Offices of Enma.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:31.990
From now on, please be careful.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:41.800
"The Offices of Enma's... First Chief of Staff."

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:48.300
Go Home, Crane

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:54.180
Note: A reference to the folk tale "The Crane that Returned the Favor."
I wonder if she'll come tonight...

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:55.680
What do you mean?

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:59.230
Well, she's a crane, right? And you saved her, right?

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:03.440
To think you actually got
the opportunity to save a crane in Hell...

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:07.150
A crane... A crane, huh?

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:09.870
What's the matter?

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:16.040
Well, I recently heard
a strange rumor that seems relevant.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:18.080
How'd the rumor go again...?

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.880
But, it's a beautiful woman who's supposed
to come and return the favor, right?

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:23.500
Nothing bad about that, right?

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:27.050
I have no time to leisurely chat about this.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.050
I'm not an old man, after all.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:31.050
Huh?

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:35.100
When the male involved
in these kinds of stories isn't an old man,

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:39.520
if the animal that was saved transforms
into a woman and pays him a visit,

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:40.400
then...

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:44.150
it's an omen that she is to become his wife.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:49.150
In other words, if the crane turns
into a woman and comes to visit me,

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:55.200
if I put her up for even a single night,
that acts as proof I've accepted the woman as my wife,

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:59.500
and our marriage will thereby be established.

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:02.250
There's no need to use that kind of reasoning...

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:06.760
It's a one hundred percent sure thing
that she intends to repay the favor, right?

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:12.760
Nowadays, I don't think a crane would come
with the intention of serving you for a lifetime, though.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:51.590
Please let me stay the night here.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:56.890
Don't shut the door!

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.970
If you're peddling English teaching materials,
we have enough already.

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:00.270
I'm not here to sell anything!

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:02.190
Can't you tell by how I'm dressed?!

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:03.770
Don't shut me out!

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:05.610
At least let me introduce myself!

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.820
My name is O-Tsu and-

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.410
I don't need any cloth either.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:21.000
Note: In the folk tale, the crane weaves beautiful fabic for the old man
who saved her.
You're skipping over lots of stuff
and ruining the story with a spoiler!

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:23.080
What is it you don't like about me?!

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:24.710
My face?! My voice?!

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:27.630
I don't really mind your face...

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:34.130
But I didn't expect a woman with
the air of a crane to come, so I'm a bit taken aback.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:37.260
Don't lock me out!

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:39.220
I just want to return the favor!

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:44.060
Even if you were to pluck your own feathers and weave,
I'd honestly find it tiresome.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:48.570
Modern-day youngsters are so quick
to say something is "tiresome"!

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:52.320
Well, I'm not a modern-day youngster, you know.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.860
Then, don't shut me out!

00:16:55.030 --> 00:17:00.160
I'm telling you that I refuse to accept anything made
by tearing off parts of your own body.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:05.330
What's with this guy? This is a carrot-and-stick approach?

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:10.630
Just when I think you've saved me only
to push me away, you show concern for my body.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:12.970
You sure make some strong assumptions.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:18.050
First off, if a woman with a mid-18th-century
unswept hairdo shows up in the middle of the night

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:21.890
holding marriage registration papers,
even if she is beautiful,

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:24.180
ninety percent of guys will be on their guard, you know.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:26.650
Well, be one of the other ten percent, then!

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:28.520
It'll be fine - just open up!

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:29.900
JUST OPEN UP FOR A SEC!

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:34.650
When you insistently show up with the kind of
determination you have, it puts people off, you know.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:39.320
Open up! If you take me as your bride,
you'll see for yourself!

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.950
I'd be a good wife, okay?!

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.000
Ah...

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:53.550
You rescued a crane...

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:56.840
So it's the customary practice...

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:02.470
to welcome the woman who shows up afterward...

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:03.270
Ouch!

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:08.060
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow...!

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:11.060
It hurts! It hurts! Ouch! Ouch!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:15.070
My fingers are caught in the door!

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:21.240
By the way, even if a pushy salesperson
gets their fingers caught in the door...
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts...!

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:21.830
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts...!

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:26.120
and even if that causes a long-lasting injury,
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts...!

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:28.710
I'm the kind of guy who thinks
there's no helping such a thing.
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts...!

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:34.380
I get it. I get it. I'll pull my fingers out,
so just crack the door open a bit more.

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:37.510
That hurt!

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:43.220
You...

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.020
Come on...

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:47.430
Look, the wound's really bad.

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:49.650
Open up and see for yourself.

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:50.940
I don't want to see it.

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:55.400
I'm the very definition of damaged goods now!

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:57.280
I'm going to make you pay my medical expenses!

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:00.280
Sign this note of assurance!

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:04.450
Come on! Come on! Come on! Come on...

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:05.040
MARRIAGE
REGISTRATION

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:14.880
At this point, it's time for my last resort.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:21.050
I get it. I understand, okay? I'm heading home,
so let me at least properly thank you first.

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:24.970
I'm going to weave!

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:30.100
If you don't at least let me do that,
I'll be violating the ways of my kin.

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:41.240
I've brought a collapsible loom with me.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.660
Once I'm done weaving, I'll head home, okay?

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:50.290
I may have said this and that,
but when a man is served to this degree,

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.000
there can't be a single one who finds it unpleasant.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:56.500
Furthermore, when someone actually lays eyes
on a traditional crane cloth,

00:19:56.500 --> 00:20:01.260
the product is so beautiful they can't help but want it.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.550
In addition...

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:09.600
Nowadays, that kind of brilliant
family-oriented skill is considered a plus.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:18.730
Yep, you're a crane, alright.

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:20.530
That's right! So don't open the door!

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:22.150
Isn't that supposed to be an unspoken agreement?!

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:25.070
What's with this guy?!
He must be messed up in the head!

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.490
I've had enough!

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:28.370
Kyaaa!

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:35.040
Mr. Hozuki!

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.670
Good evening. What's the matter?

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:42.300
I've remembered...

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:46.510
About that strange rumor I mentioned this afternoon
that I heard from a fellow bird friend.

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:52.310
These days, there's even a marriage-hunting
community solely for birds, you see...

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:57.310
Birds will showily pretend that they're in trouble
in hopes that someone will come to their rescue.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:01.030
Then when they ascertain that they've found
a prominent man, they make their move.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:04.320
Basically, I'm saying that there are
some nasty hens out there!

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:16.920
Eye Pecking Realm Sponsored
Marriage-hunting Party
For Birds

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:17.170
You're lucky to be a crane since you're able
to use the strategy of "the crane returns the favor."

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:21.170
Oh, I wouldn't say that. It just failed me yet again.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:24.630
There simply aren't any good men out there.

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:28.010
But, you know, it's really something that,
on top of using that strategy,

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:30.010
you've also come to a marriage-hunting party.

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:32.680
Don't you think you're being a bit indiscriminate?

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:36.190
Well, I place a lot of importance
on the guy's annual income.

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:41.230
But, in truth, it's a turn off
if the guy's not a perceptive observer.

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:42.400
MARRIAGE
REGISTRATION

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:44.400
Aww...

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:48.570
What's the matter, Mr. Hozuki?

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:53.250
In short, she's an accident faker, isn't she?

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:10.600
Uso yo. Janakya naze koko ni tadoritsuku no?
That's a lie. If not, why do you find your way here?

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:17.230
Enma-sama no mae de nao shira o kiru no ne
Even in front of Lord Enma, you feign ignorance

00:22:17.690 --> 00:22:23.150
Baka ne. Dakedo sonna toko tamaranakute
You're an idiot. But I can't get enough of that aspect of you

00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:29.530
Teitaraku. Onaji tsumi kasanetsuzuketa
What a predicament. You continued to repeat the same sin

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:34.830
Ii no? Yubikiri genman.
Is that alright? Pinky swear.

00:22:34.830 --> 00:22:36.200
(E?)
(Huh?)
Ii no? Yubikiri genman.
Is that alright? Pinky swear.

00:22:36.710 --> 00:22:41.040
Gachi ni honto ni naru yo.
It will seriously become reality.

00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:42.630
(Dogii!)
(Startling!)
Gachi ni honto ni naru yo.
It will seriously become reality.

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:49.050
Tensei o matazu shounetsu no mama ni
Without waiting for reincarnation, while still in the scorching heat

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:55.060
Asa hiru eien ai o kushizashi narabete
Morning, midday, and eternally skewer desires and line them up

00:22:55.310 --> 00:22:58.230
Gutsu gutsu mou! Nie nie da yo
Already simmering! It's boiling

00:22:58.480 --> 00:23:01.650
Yuuge wa jigoku de hot pot
Supper is a hot pot in Hell

00:23:01.810 --> 00:23:07.860
Nita mono doushi ni oniai no oshioki
For people who are alike, a suitable punishment

00:23:08.030 --> 00:23:10.990
Juu juu achi! Koge koge da yo
Sizzling hot! It's burned to a crisp

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:14.280
Anata to jigoku de hotcake
Hotcakes with you in Hell

00:23:14.450 --> 00:23:19.710
Tokoyo no suna ni naru made
Until they become forever-unchanging sand

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:26.670
NEXT TIME
ON HOZUKI'S
COOLHEADEDNESS...

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:28.630
There sure are all kinds of yokai in Hell, you know?

00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:28.840
AND

00:23:28.630 --> 00:23:30.970
Like the Zashiki Warashi, Nekomata, and so on.

00:23:29.590 --> 00:23:30.130
BUT

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:32.340
It appears Nurarihyon is here, too.

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:34.890
Him or the Nine-Tailed Fox, which is stronger?

00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:33.760
SO

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:38.520
I wonder... If you're looking to  neglect your work,
I'll feed you to the Nine-Tailed Fox, you know.

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:39.730
WE PRESENT:
SLIPPERY AS A CATISH
AND
GON GETS TO WORK

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:39.730
PLEASE ENJOY!

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:39.600
I'll work...
